# Paths cited in load-bearing docs that may not exist on disk.
# One path per line. Empty lines + lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Use cases:
#  - Forward references to planned-but-not-built files.
#  - Historical references to files deleted by lifecycle policy
#    (e.g. completed plans removed per `feedback_plan_lifecycle` memory).
#
# Every entry should explain WHY in a comment. Drift checked: when an entry's
# file actually exists on disk, the cite-check warns to remove the allowlist
# row.
